  "note": "From the County Clerk-Recorder's zero summary report for the November 3, 2026 election, which lists every contest on the county's ballots. No Board of Supervisors seat, Sheriff, District Attorney or other county office, no Superior Court judge, and no countywide measure is on this ballot. City of San Luis Obispo council members are now elected by citywide single vote: each voter picks one candidate and the top two are elected. Not shown: mayor and council contests in other cities (Arroyo Grande, Atascadero, Grover Beach, Morro Bay, Paso Robles, Pismo Beach), community college, school, community services and special districts, congressional and legislative districts, and city, school and college measures (A-26 and C-26 through H-26). Incumbent flags are not set because no official roster could be checked. Statewide races and the Supreme Court retention are on the California statewide list. Check your official sample ballot for district contests.",
